ZVSE2

** CHAT FIX - runs BEFORE "easy cheats.erm" (Easy Cheats mod)
**
** Easy Cheats treats every chat text that is not a cheat as an ERM command or an ERM variable to show
** (a debug console). Normal text like "Death Stare" is read as a variable and gives an ERM error.
** Here such text is cleared before Easy Cheats reads it. Kept: cheats (handled before this function),
** ERM commands (contain ':'), and variables like v1, y-5, z12, i^name^, a(name).
**
** Also: the chat event sometimes comes with no text at all (address 0), and Easy Cheats reads it without
** checking ("SN:B - cannot read/write to zero address"). The address is replaced by an empty string.

!#DC(CHAT_FIX_EMPTY_STRING) = 6687262;  [660A1E: a zero byte in h3era.exe = empty string]

!?FU(OnChat)&x1=(CHAT_EVENT_TYPE_INPUT)/i^cr_hasEasyCheats^;
!#VA(action:x) (strAddr:x) (result:x);
!!VR(strAddr)&(strAddr)=0:S(CHAT_FIX_EMPTY_STRING);

!?FU(ech_ProcessCmd)&i^cr_hasEasyCheats^;
!#VA(cmdPtr:x);

!!VR(input:z):Sz(cmdPtr);
!!FU&(input)=^^:E;

!!FU(StrPos):P(input)/^:^/?(pos:y);
!!FU&(pos)>=0:E;                         [ERM command]
!!FU(StrPos):P(input)/^%\"^/?(pos);
!!FU&(pos)>=0:E;                         [named variable like i^name^]
!!FU(StrPos):P(input)/^(^/?(pos);
!!FU&(pos)>=0:E;                         [array like a(name)]

; Variables like v1, y-5, z12: a letter followed by a digit or '-'
!!VR(input):M4/?(length:y);
!!if&(length)>=2;
  !!SN:K(input)/1/?(secondChar:y);
  !!FU&(secondChar)>=48/(secondChar)<=57:E;   [0-9]
  !!FU&(secondChar)=45:E;                     [-]
!!en;

; Normal chat text: ignore it
!!VRz(cmdPtr):S^^;
